{
  "name": "What to Expect During a Hail Damage Roof Repair Evaluation in Alliance",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1: Initial Storm and Roof History Review — We'll start by discussing the recent hailstorm, your roof's age, and any prior repairs or known issues. This background helps us understand the context of the current damage and identify potential weak spots. We'll also ask about your insurance policy to understand the claims process.",
      "text": "Step 1: Initial Storm and Roof History Review — We'll start by discussing the recent hailstorm, your roof's age, and any prior repairs or known issues. This background helps us understand the context of the current damage and identify potential weak spots. We'll also ask about your insurance policy to understand the claims process.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 2: Ground-Level Safety Survey — Before anyone steps foot on your roof, our team conducts a safety check from the ground. This ensures it's safe to access and prevents further damage during the inspection. We look for obvious hazards and make note of visible damage from below.",
      "text": "Step 2: Ground-Level Safety Survey — Before anyone steps foot on your roof, our team conducts a safety check from the ground. This ensures it's safe to access and prevents further damage during the inspection. We look for obvious hazards and make note of visible damage from below.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 2
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 3: Comprehensive Roof and Component Inspection — We'll then carefully inspect every slope of your roof. This includes documenting impact marks with photos, assessing granule loss, bruising, cracking, or punctures on your shingles. We also check other crucial components like underlayment, flashings, vents, valleys, gutters, and related exterior surfaces that hail might have affected.",
      "text": "Step 3: Comprehensive Roof and Component Inspection — We'll then carefully inspect every slope of your roof. This includes documenting impact marks with photos, assessing granule loss, bruising, cracking, or punctures on your shingles. We also check other crucial components like underlayment, flashings, vents, valleys, gutters, and related exterior surfaces that hail might have affected.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 3
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 4: Damage Documentation and Assessment — As we inspect, we'll take detailed photos and notes, often using scale markers to show the size of hail impacts. We'll classify the severity and location of damage. For repair evaluations, we often use representative test areas to understand the extent of damage across different parts of the roof.",
      "text": "Step 4: Damage Documentation and Assessment — As we inspect, we'll take detailed photos and notes, often using scale markers to show the size of hail impacts. We'll classify the severity and location of damage. For repair evaluations, we often use representative test areas to understand the extent of damage across different parts of the roof.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 4
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 5: Repair vs. Replacement Recommendation and Estimate — Based on our findings, we'll discuss whether isolated repairs are appropriate or if a roof section or full replacement is needed. We'll explain our reasoning, distinguishing between repairable conditions and damage that truly affects your roof's long-term performance. You'll receive a clear scope of work and a detailed estimate.",
      "text": "For a transparent hail damage roof repair evaluation in Alliance, contact Discounted Roofing Co. today.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 5
    }
  ],
